Amplitude $50$, centre line $P = 400$, period $\dfrac{2\pi}{\pi/6} = 12$ months, so exactly one cycle:
- maximum $450$ at $t = 0$ and $t = 12$;
- minimum $350$ at $t = 6$;
- $P = 400$ (centre line) at $t = 3$ and $t = 9$;
- $P = 375$ at $t = 4$ and $t = 8$ (from part (i)).

Amplitude $3$, period $\dfrac{2\pi}{1/2} = 4\pi$, so the interval $-2\pi \le x \le 2\pi$ shows exactly one cycle:
- $x$-intercepts at $x = -2\pi, 0, 2\pi$;
- minimum $(-\pi, -3)$ and maximum $(\pi, 3)$.
